<p>I think there's a difference. Also I like this a lot, and I like it pretty much purely for the journal.</p>
<p>The telepathic spider was about a spider getting wigged out when it was talking to the equivalent of eldritch beings from beyond the veil (and said beings actually sympathizing with the spider on account of also dealing with things that are equally beyond their own ability to understand).</p>
<p>This is also about a researcher trying to understand what the butterfly is transmitting&#8230; but it seems like the researcher is overwhelmed by the content rather than understanding it.</p>
<p>I think the ultimate idea here is that suffering is lessened by sharing it with others. The butterfly is not feeding, it's sharing. But if you take on too much, you'll be crippled by it like the researcher was.</p>
<p>edit: also it's kinda neat that the telepathic bugs are so close together in the list completely by coincidence.</p>

